WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.150
. David, Donald Trump is increasingly talking
about.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.779
Giving businesses immunity from Corona virus
related lawsuits.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:14.800
Does this make sense or should employees always
be able to sue, sue and seek damages from

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.299
their employer?

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:22.300
If they were to catch Corona virus as a result
of being back at work?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:28.269
Listen, this is really a complicated issue
from a practic, from a logistical sense, from

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:33.890
a legal sense, where you have to understand,
well, what is the current liability that employers

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:34.890
have?

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:41.670
Is catching Corona virus the same as an unsafe
warehouse where you get run over by a forklift

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.100
because the forklift didn't make the beeping
noise and have the red light that it's supposed

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.210
to have and steel toed shoes weren't requite.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.210
Right.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:55.370
These are these are very different questions
when it comes to something like Corona virus.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:03.800
If you go to work and you catch Corona virus
and everybody was behaving safely and the

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:11.499
employer has opened in accordance with CDC
guidelines, foreign state guidelines for OK,

00:01:11.499 --> 00:01:16.909
employees need masks and the employees had
masks, there should be X number of sanitation's.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:22.250
They if all the rules are being adhered to
and people catch corona virus.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:29.299
It's very difficult to say that the employer
should be liable for that, particularly when

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:35.280
the contagion may have happened because of
some random customer or who knows.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.179
It's a very difficult legal question.

00:01:38.179 --> 00:01:42.409
But should there be some blanket immunity
for employers?

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:43.509
Of course not.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:44.689
Of course not.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:53.039
We have an infrastructure for determining
when an employer is or is not liable for something

00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:57.290
that happens to an employee or to a customer
on the premises.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.039
It is very robust legislation.

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:00.960
It is very established.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.119
There is no shortage of cases of all kinds
about employers who failed to protect employees

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:09.790
and customers or who were sued.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:13.070
But it was determined they actually did take
the proper precautions.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:18.860
The danger here is that for political reasons
and for the purposes of furthering what is

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:26.000
become a culture war overgrown virus, Donald
Trump is seeking to give blanket immunity

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.880
for anything corona virus related that happens
in their place of business when they reopen.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:39.160
And what this is really about is employers
who are not following the guidelines that

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:44.730
Trump wants to see have immunity so that they
will just open up even when it is not yet

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.980
safe to do so on the basis of the guidelines
that have been put in place.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.550
This is about Trump wanting to give a carte
blanche sort of situation to employers that

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.550
want to reopen.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.240
And even though the state says you need masks,
they don't want their employees to wear masks

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.700
and in some cases may even tell their employees
no masks whatsoever.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:08.910
So for me, the last thing we need is any blanket
immunity for employers.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:15.110
But I am sensitive to the reality that your
employer can be doing the right thing and

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:20.360
you might get coronavirus versus your employer
might not be doing the right thing.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.870
Those are the situations that need to be adjudicated.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.760
Listen, here's the reality.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.310
If you're an essential worker at a grocery
store and you continue working.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.970
We know that the longer you are in places
where the virus is circulating, your odds

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.250
of contracting it go way, way up.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.220
Spending 15 minutes with a mask on at Trader
Joe's.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:43.550
Even if there are people in there with the
virus is not hugely likely to end up with

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:49.790
you getting the virus, spending eight hours
a day, five or six days a week there, even

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.960
with a mask dramatically, still sees an increase
in the chance that you get it.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.870
Does that mean the employer is acting inappropriately
and should be sued?

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.260
No, not necessarily.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.680
What I do think is that essential workers
should be compensated additionally for the

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.530
fact that they are essential and are often
some of the least well-paid people.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.050
That's a battle I'll have all day long.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:16.670
But if employers really are being safe, we
have a system that would adjudicate that and

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.280
would say this lawsuit has no merit.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.770
The employer did the right thing.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:21.889
Everybody did the right thing.

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:24.020
We have a contagious situation.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.210
If grocery stores should have been closed,
that's a bigger governmental call that should

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.400
have been made.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.900
But we don't need any special dispensation,
as the case may be, from Donald Trump or the

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:41.120
federal government to shield a Priore employers,
because employers may take advantage of that

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.570
and some will take advantage of it to have
deliberately unsafe conditions that they believe

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.970
are better for them in the short and maybe
medium term.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.080
You could say, listen, over the long term,
if all your employees get sick and a bunch

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.340
of them die, it's bad for PR.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.860
You're not going to have employees.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.770
OK, there are lots of industries that have
such turnover as it is that they regularly

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.201
have a stable of applicants and they can bring
people in.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.930
Quickly and trained them relatively quickly
for relatively unskilled labor.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.540
Many businesses would not really be concerned
about that.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.660
So no blanket immunity.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:16.520
We have a system that can determine, is this
a valid claim or is this what we would call

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.830
a frivolous claim?

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.720
They don't need any special bailout.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.040
It's part of the culture war.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:27.900
It's part of this haphazard desire to open
the economy fully, immediately, regardless

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.431
of what the repercussions are.

00:05:29.431 --> 00:05:35.810
In my experience, any blanket immunities for
corporations from future lawsuits are bad

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:36.810
news.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.740
I am open to the idea that sometimes they
are OK.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.000
I looked today for examples.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.370
Couldn't find any.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.370
Couldn't find any.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.080
If you have an example.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.080
Absolutely.

